<TUTORIALS>
 <TUTORIAL ID="1" NAME="tutorial.area.enter" CAPTION="Guest Areas">
   <DESC><![CDATA[You're in a VMK guest area. To get around, click on the area of the ground you'd like to walk to. You'll find exits at the edges of the room, marked with a red cursor. If you want to learn more about the room you're in, click on the 'Room Info' button.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.navigation.walking</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="2" NAME="tutorial.camera.open" CAPTION="Taking Photos">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Capture your adventures in VMK with this camera. Simply click 'Take Photo' in the Camera menu and then line up your shot. Don't forget to add a caption, so you remember the moment!]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.explore.photos</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="3" NAME="tutorial.catalog.open" CAPTION="Buy New Stuff">
   <DESC><![CDATA[This is where you buy new stuff, with the credits you've made by playing the games. You can get clothing, pins, posters, furniture or film for your camera. Collect more pages for your Catalog by visiting the shops - every land has one!]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.stuff.credits</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="4" NAME="tutorial.emotes.open" CAPTION="Use Emotes in Chat">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Emotes are a quick way to express your feelings. Just double click the Mickey face that suits your mood and it will show up in the room. You can also wave to your friends by clicking the 'Wave' button, or dance while you chat by clicking 'Dance'.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.chat.emotes</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="5" NAME="tutorial.friend.request" CAPTION="Making Friends">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Making someone your friend lets them send you messages, and find out what VMK room you're in. You can always remove someone from you list if you don't feel like being friends anymore.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.messaging.friends</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="6" NAME="tutorial.furniture.place" CAPTION="Furnishing Your Room">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Once you've found the right place, you can rotate your furniture. You can also move it somewhere else or click to 'Take Away'. You only see these options when you have selected the 'Furnishing Mode' in the 'Room Info' window.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.rooms.furnish</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="7" NAME="tutorial.help.open" CAPTION="Find More Help">
   <DESC><![CDATA[If you need more information about the game, just browse through the topic menus. If you're having trouble with another player and need help from VMK Staff right away, click the 'Call For Help' button.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.about.safety</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="8" NAME="tutorial.inventory.open" CAPTION="Manage Your Stuff">
   <DESC><![CDATA[This is where you view and manage your stuff. You can choose furniture and posters to place in your room, and change the pins you're wearing. If you have a secret code, go to the 'Codes' tab to get your reward.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.stuff.codes</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="9" NAME="tutorial.magic.open" CAPTION="Perform Magic">
   <DESC><![CDATA[You can only perform magic if you're wearing a magic pin. Simply double-click on your pin in the 'Magic' menu (or use the 'magic word' in chat). Click 'Stop' to end the effect. You have to wait for a while after using a magic effect to restore your powers.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.about.magic</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="10" NAME="tutorial.message.receive" CAPTION="Messages">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Make sure you read and reply to your message before you click 'Next', otherwise it will be deleted before you get a chance to. If you get a message that worries you, you can report it to VMK Staff and remove the sender from your friend list.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.messaging.guide</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="11" NAME="tutorial.messenger.open" CAPTION="Use the Messenger">
   <DESC><![CDATA[This is where you manage your friend list - you can send and accept requests, and remove people from your list. Once someone's on your friend list, you can send them messages or go to same room to chat.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.messaging.guide</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="12" NAME="tutorial.navigator.guest" CAPTION="Go to a Guest Room">
   <DESC><![CDATA[The guest rooms are created by other players. You can see the most popular rooms and the rooms of all of your online friends. The 'Own Rooms' tab will take you straight to your own room, where you can get busy furnishing, or host your own visitors.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.navigation.navigator</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="13" NAME="tutorial.navigator.land" CAPTION="Go to a Guest Area">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Click the name of a guest area to enter it. If you use Advanced Navigation, you'll have to choose an 'instance'. All of the instances look the same but you'll find different people in each one. If one instance (e.g. 'South') is full, try another.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.navigation.navigator</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="14" NAME="tutorial.navigator.open" CAPTION="Get Around the Kingdom">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Click a land to discover new guest areas and games. Or select the 'Guest Rooms' tab for a shortcut to your own and other players' rooms. Only select the Advanced Navigation Mode if you're a true VMK pro and you want to navigate to a specific instance.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.navigation.navigator</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="15" NAME="tutorial.photo.open" CAPTION="Manage Your Photos">
   <DESC><![CDATA[The photo catalog includes all of the pictures you've taken and saved. You can edit your photo captions, or choose a picture to place on the wall of your room. If you've bought a photo album from VMK Central, you can use it to show off your collection.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.explore.photos</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="16" NAME="tutorial.poster.place" CAPTION="Place a Poster">
   <DESC><![CDATA[The poster is now attached to your cursor. Move your cursor around to find the right place on your guest room wall. The poster becomes see-thru if you move it over areas it can't stick to.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.rooms.furnish</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="17" NAME="tutorial.profile.open" CAPTION="Player Profiles">
   <DESC><![CDATA[You have opened another player's profile. This will show their VMK name, signature and the pins they're wearing. There are also some options for you: you can start a trade with them, ask them to be your friend, or ignore them if they're causing trouble.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.characters.badges</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="18" NAME="tutorial.room.enter" CAPTION="Guest Rooms">
   <DESC><![CDATA[This room is owned and furnished by a player like you. You can chat and make friends with the owner, and play the games they organise. But remember that you're a guest to their room so be nice if you don't want to be kicked out!]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.about.values</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="19" NAME="tutorial.room.info" CAPTION="Room Information">
   <DESC><![CDATA[The 'Room Info' will show the 'instance' you're in (e.g. 'South'), so you can tell other players exactly where you are. Each area in VMK can have many instances. All of the instances of an area look the same but you'll find different people in each one.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.navigation.navigator</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="20" NAME="tutorial.settings.open" CAPTION="Change Your Image">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Change the look of your character by choosing a new hairstyle or trying on the clothing you've bought. You can also update the 'signature' that other people see when they look at your profile. You change your pins from your 'Stuff' menu.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.character.pins</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="21" NAME="tutorial.shop.enter" CAPTION="Shops">
   <DESC><![CDATA[You're in a shop! Click on the cash register to get a Catalog page full of new items (and maybe even some special offers). You can get to the other shops via a Teleporter - simply walk into one to be instantly transported.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.explore.shops</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
 <TUTORIAL ID="22" NAME="tutorial.trade.request" CAPTION="Trade With Another Player">
   <DESC><![CDATA[Another player wants to trade with you! They will offer you some of the items they own and you can choose what you want to give them in exchange. Chat about it as you go. Nothing is final until you check the 'Accept' box.]]></DESC>
   <LINK>help.stuff.trading</LINK>
 </TUTORIAL>
</TUTORIALS>